  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 114 PM MDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nUpper high drifts south and weakens slowly Mon/Tue, before\ngradually shifting eastward into srn plains from Wed into the \nend of the week. Moisture increases slowly at first, with a \ngradual ramp up of convection across the mountains Mon/Tue as \nmid-level moisture works eastward around the high. Temps will \nremain hot, though readings will likely drift slowly downward \neach day as mid-level heights/temps fall. More substantial \ninflux of moisture expected from mid to late week as high moves \nfar enough east to allow flow to become more sly, bringing back \na fairly classic late summer monsoon pattern to the region. \nModels/ensembles hint a potential front on the plains late week \nas well, with low level moisture surging westward toward the \nmountains. Looks like a wet/active period Thu into the weekend \nas a result, and heavy rain/flash flooding will likely become a \nconcern, especially over fresh mountain burn scars.",
